Only the emulator core is copied: the host platform layers (os_*_posix.c,
os_window_x11.c, ...), main.c, the x64/arm64 asm backends, ROMs and datasheets
are not. The RP2350 platform layer lives in src/machines/beeb (with src/common and
src/boards/presto).

Local changes, for the RP2350 port (2026), mostly behind BEEBJIT_* defines so
that the default (upstream) build is unchanged:

- asm/thumb2/ (new): a Thumb-2 (Cortex-M33) JIT and inturbo backend;
  asm_*.c and asm_platform.h select it with BEEBJIT_ASM_THUMB2.
  jit_metadata.c marks the 6502 pages that have JIT code, so stores elsewhere
  skip the invalidation lookup.
- jit.c, jit_compiler.c: BEEBJIT_JIT_COMPACT (per-page fixups and a bounded
  history cache, in the host's big memory via BEEBJIT_MALLOC_BIG); no x86 TLB
  alignment padding for the thumb2 backend.
- bbc.c: BEEBJIT_NO_MMU (flat memory, ROM writes dropped, sideways RAM written
  by bbc_write_callback); bbc_request_reset() and a host reset hook;
  bbc_replace_disc() (writeable and mutable on request: a writes-back drive
  for the host's save disc); bbc_swap_roms().
- disc.c, disc_ssd.c, disc_drive.c: BEEBJIT_DISC_COMPACT (tracks allocated,
  and .ssd/.dsd tracks built, when the drive first reaches them);
  disc_drive_replace_discs().
- video.c, render.c, teletext.c, timing.c, interp.c: BEEBJIT_RENDER_PACKED4
  (4-bit packed pixels), row mode (render_set_row_buffer()),
  BEEBJIT_VIDEO_FAST_RUNS (whole scanlines and character rows at a time),
  BEEBJIT_RENDER_WIRE (render calls sent to another core),
  BEEBJIT_INTERP_COUNTDOWN32.
- debug.c: the per-address counters made only when stats are turned on, the
  struct in the big memory.
- keyboard.c/.h: keyboard_bbc_key_to_rowcol() public. serial_ula.c/.h:
  serial_ula_is_motor_on().
- util.c: BEEBJIT_MALLOC / BEEBJIT_REALLOC / BEEBJIT_FREE hooks.
- sound.c: BEEBJIT_SOUND_WRITE_HOOK (each byte the SN76489 takes, with its
  timer ticks, handed to the host's own sound: src/common/sound.c).
- state.c, debug.c: int32_t where int was passed as int32_t* (an upstream
  portability bug where int32_t is long).
- Added from upstream, unmodified: test-*.c (included by their modules),
  os_fault_platform_null.c (with carry/overflow for the thumb2 JIT) and
  os_sound_null.c.
